  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1139 AM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nA band of moderate to locally heavy rain is progressing eastward \ninto eastern MN and northwest WI late this morning. Rainfall totals \nhave been in the 1/4 to 1/2 inch range, but some areas have had \naround 3/4 inch such as in Alexandria. The showers will eventually \nfocus in western WI later this afternoon as the mid level trough \nswings through with just a few light showers lingering in MN into \nearly evening. Mid and high level clouds will move out this evening. \nWith the surface front remaining well to the north until later \nWednesday, ample low level moisture will remain in place. Fog \ndevelopment tonight is expected, especially in areas where low \nlevel cloud depth becomes quite shallow. This is most probable \nacross central and western MN which would be furthest removed \nfrom the trough axis, and the moisture transport ribbon from the\nsouthern Plains to mid Mississippi Valley. Some of the fog may \nbecome dense.\n\nA warm and humid airmass will be in place Wednesday ahead of an \napproaching cold front later in the day. 925 mb temps will range \nfrom +18C to +21C, so highs in the mid to upper 70s are likely \nwith an 80 not being ruled out in a few places. Early morning \nfog should burn off by mid to late morning. Dry air aloft and \nthe shallow moist layer at the surface will be able to keep the \nfog from transitioning to low stratus that is more difficult to \nscatter out. Increased temperatures closer to the NBM 75th \npercentile.\n\nA quiet zonal flow pattern will dominate the first week of October. \nThis will keep temperatures mild and precip chances to a minimum. \nSurface high pressure building in Friday may allow for one of the \ncooler nights of the week Friday night and some patchy frost \nformation is possible over northern MN/WI. Quick on the heels of the \ndeparture of the surface high will be a somewhat vigorous short\nwave Saturday afternoon and evening, bringing our only chance \nof showers in the extended period.",
